        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d0c74191-f31f-52a5-a21b-c5971b133929",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Clarence Brown, Peter Glenville, Sidney Franklin, Cara Duff-MacCormick, Michael York\n- Works: The Yearling, Out Cry\n- Roles: film director, actor, stage director, producer\n- Organizations: Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer\n\nFacts:\n- Clarence Brown was born on May 10, 1890, and he was an American film director.\n- Peter Glenville, born Peter Patrick Brabazon Browne, was born on 28 October 1913, and he was an English film and stage actor and director.\n- The Yearling is a 1946 Technicolor family film drama directed by Clarence Brown, produced by Sidney Franklin, and released by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.\n- The Yearling is about a young boy who adopts a trouble-making young deer.\n- A New York production of Out Cry was directed by Peter Glenville and starred Cara Duff-MacCormick as Clare and Michael York as Felice.\n- Peter Glenville died on 3 June 1996.\n- Clarence Brown died on August 17, 1987.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
